-- ===== FRONT (five pairs): public.gmo_kline_files -> us(symbol, ot, seq, m8, d), the 15-minute series production judges on =====
-- instrument table: GMO symbol, the app's pair name, display order, the instant from which the v7 rule (signal-alerts v31, the 15-minute chart) was live, and the decimals
-- of the chart's rounding (decimalsOf: 3 for a ...JPY pair, 5 for the others):
-- 1793009700000 = 2026-10-26 10:15 UTC (go-live, live_ms): the open of the first 15-minute bar v31 judged. v31 was put out at once, in the middle of GMO day 20261026
-- (pull request #245 merged 10:23:24 UTC, signal-alerts deployed 10:23:51.752 UTC = its updated_at; the six subscriptions were '15min' by 10:25:01 at the latest, read from
-- gold's sweep reads, and certainly at 10:29:36). The pairs' 15-minute charts are read at minutes m % 15 in {0, 1, 3} (gmoIntervalsDue), so the first v31 read was at
-- 10:30 and judged the bar opened 10:15; the bar opened 10:00 (read 10:15 to 10:18, by v30, which had no 15-minute macdx chart) was never judged. To move it: change
-- the number here and in syms-gold-v7.part, rebuild (bash build.sh) and say so in README.md section v7.1.
syms as (
  select * from (values
    ('USD_JPY', 'USD/JPY', 1, 1793009700000::bigint, 3), ('EUR_JPY', 'EUR/JPY', 2, 1793009700000::bigint, 3), ('AUD_JPY', 'AUD/JPY', 3, 1793009700000::bigint, 3),
    ('EUR_USD', 'EUR/USD', 4, 1793009700000::bigint, 5), ('AUD_USD', 'AUD/USD', 5, 1793009700000::bigint, 5)
  ) v(symbol, pair, ord, live_ms, d)
),
